<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trieu Quang Phuc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 571</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Triệu Quang Phục, Trieu Viet Vuong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trieu Quang Phuc was a Vietnamese leader who continued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-nam-de">Ly Bi</a>'s resistance to the Liang dynasty after 546, waging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war from the Da Trach marshes. After Chinese forces withdrew he ruled the Red River delta as Trieu Viet Vuong. He was overthrown in 571 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-phat-tu">Ly Phat Tu</a>, a relative of Ly Bi.</p></div>
